{
  "question": "After prescriber approval, what code clears a Part D 90-MME alert? Do our documents specify one?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "Assuming Medicare Part D (90-MME care coordination edit).",
  "answer": "Assuming Medicare Part D: **No, the documents don't specify a code.** The CMS pharmacist guide (12/19/2022) says to consult the prescriber, document the discussion (date, time, prescriber name, brief note), and \"submit the appropriate override code.\" It doesn't name the code, such as an NCPDP DUR/PPS value. It also says plans must allow POS overrides of all opioid alerts, and that overrides for exemptions go \"with a transaction code or by contacting the plan directly.\"\n\nGet the exact code from the plan's payer sheet or the plan itself. No specific value appears in these documents.\n\nIf a recent prescriber consult and current PDMP data are already in hand, repeat consultation isn't expected.",
